--- body ---

## Context

Reported from the arena (arena ticket 1111, Q3 smoke leg 0338-f1b, 2026-11-01, harness pin
night-pins/2026-11-01-q3-smoke, harness 4782cf0c). The arena runs the harness as installed by
`idh install` in a sealed HOME. A Pi contestant called the subagent tool for `gate-seat` and got
`Unknown agent: ... Available agents: none`.

Observations (cause not checked beyond reading the code):

1. Pi's subagent extension (`agents.ts`, `discoverAgents`) reads user agents from
   `getAgentDir()/agents` (`$PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR/agents`, default `~/.pi/agent/agents`); the project
   scope (`.pi/agents` above the cwd) is opt-in per call (`agentScope`). The installed HOME links
   `agents/*.md` into `~/.claude/agents` only; `~/.pi/agent/` receives no `agents/`. So on Pi the
   harness roles (gate-seat, coder, team-lead, prose-reviewer, code-reviewer) are not delegable.
2. `adapters/pi/agents/` holds only `code-reviewer.md` (Pi tool names). The runtime-neutral
   `agents/*.md` declare Claude tool names (`tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Write`); the extension
   passes them to the child as `--tools Read,Grep,Glob,Bash,Write`. Whether Pi maps these to its
   `read, grep, find, ls, bash, write` tools or drops them is not verified.
3. `skills/route/routes.json` declares no `local_providers` on the `pi` headless door, so
   `gaze_seat.py` treats a padme seat as cross-family spend needing consent (the leg's refusals
   were all on padme).

The arena now works around 1 on its own side, for its Q3 rung only: it links the pinned
`agents/*.md` (with `adapters/pi/agents/` winning by name) into the leg's Pi agent dir, and steps
aside if the installed home ever ships `~/.pi/agent/agents`. That makes the arena add something
the harness does not install, which a harness-side projection would remove.

## Scope

- Install-time projection of the harness agents for Pi (`~/.pi/agent/agents`), as for Claude Code.
- Pi renderings (or a tool-name mapping) for the agents whose `tools:` use Claude names.
- Decide whether padme belongs in the `pi` door's `local_providers`.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] After `idh install`, `~/.pi/agent/agents/` lists the harness agents and a Pi subagent call to
      `gate-seat` resolves.
- [ ] A Pi child launched for a harness agent gets the intended tools (test on the `--tools` value).
- [ ] The padme/local_providers decision is recorded.
